r complained. Accusation continues in verses 6–7, not merely an unspecified cry.", "reason": "lexical_alternative"}]}}, {"reference": "1 Enoch 22:6", "source": {"edition": "charles-1906-enoch", "text": "ውእቱ፡ ጊዜ፡ ተስእልክዎ፡ ለሩፋኤል፡ መልአክ፡ እንዘ፡ ሀሎ፡ ምስሌየ፡ ወእቤሎ፡ ዝመንፈስ፡ ዘመኑ፡ ውእቱ፡ ዘከመዝ፡ ቃሉ፡ ይበጽሕ፡ ወይሰኪ።", "language": "Geez", "pages": [94, 96], "confidence": "medium", "validation": "unapplied_full_printed_unit_candidate", "note": "Unapplied Charles1906 printed critical-edition candidate after first independent whole-chapter revise/hold review. Recheck actual PDF94–98 including facing apparatus on95 and97; no manuscript or human specialist certification."}, "translation": {"text": "At that time I asked Raphael, the angel who was with me, and said to him, “Whose spirit is this, whose voice reaches out in this way and makes accusation?”[a]", "philosophy": "optimal-equivalence", "footnotes": [{"marker": "a", "text": "Or complains. The particular spirit is identified as Abel’s in verse 7, which names the person accused.", "reason": "cross_reference"}]}}, {"reference": "1 Enoch 22:7", "source": {"edition": "charles-1906-enoch", "text": "ወአውሥአኒ፡ [ወይቤለኒ፡] እንዘ፡ ይብል፡ ዝንቱ፡ መንፈስ፡ ውእቱ፡ ዘ*ወጽአ፡ እምአቤል፡ ዘ*ቀተሎ፡ ቃየን፡ እኁሁ፡ ወይሰኪ፡ ኪያሁ፡ እስከ፡ ሶበ፡ ይትኀጐል፡ ዘርኡ፡ እምቅድመ፡ ገጸ፡ ለምድር፡ ወእምዘርአ፡ ሰብእ፡ ይማስን፡ ዘርኡ።", "language": "Geez", "pages": [96], "confidence": "medium", "validation": "unapplied_full_printed_unit_candidate", "note": "Unapplied Charles1906 printed critical-edition candidate after first independent whole-chapter revise/hold review. Recheck actual PDF94–98 including facing apparatus on95 and97; no manuscript or human specialist certification."}, "translation": {"text": "And he answered me, saying,[a] “This is the spirit that came out from Abel[b], whom Qayin his brother killed. It accuses him until his seed is destroyed from the face of the earth, and his seed perishes from among the seed of men.”[c]", "philosophy": "optimal-equivalence", "footnotes": [{"marker": "a", "text": "Charles brackets and said to me as a doublet of the unbracketed speech formula (printed note 6); the English omits that doublet.", "reason": "editorial_bracketing"}, {"marker": "b", "text": "The departure wording follows a starred correction in Charles note 7, not an unqualified manuscript consensus.", "reason": "editorial_emendation"}, {"marker": "c", "text": "Him and both occurrences of his seed refer to Qayin and his descendants, not to Abel.", "reason": "referent_disclosure"}]}}, {"reference": "1 Enoch 22:8", "source": {"edition": "charles-1906-enoch", "text": "ውእተ፡ ጊዜ፡ ተስእልኩ፡ [በእንቲአሁ፡ ወ]በእንተ፡ †ኵነኔ፡† ኵሉ፡ በእንተ፡ ምንት፡ ተፈልጡ፡ ፩እምነ፡ ፩።", "language": "Geez", "pages": [96], "confidence": "medium", "validation": "unapplied_full_printed_unit_candidate", "note": "Unapplied Charles1906 printed critical-edition candidate after first independent whole-chapter revise/hold review. Recheck actual PDF94–98 including facing apparatus on95 and97; no manuscript or human specialist certification."}, "translation": {"text": "At that time I asked,[a] concerning all the hollow places,[b] “Why have they been separated from one another?”", "philosophy": "optimal-equivalence", "footnotes": [{"marker": "a", "text": "Charles brackets concerning him and as an intrusion in printed note 18; the English omits it.", "reason": "editorial_bracketing"}, {"marker": "b", "text": "Hollow places follows Charles’s correction in printed note 19: the marked Ethiopic judgments corresponds to Greek κρίματα, which he regards as corrupt for κοιλώματα.", "reason": "editorial_emendation"}]}}, {"reference": "1 Enoch 22:9", "source": {"edition": "charles-1906-enoch", "text": "*ወአውሥአኒ፡ ወይቤለኒ፡ እሉ፡ ፫ተገብሩ፡ ከመ፡ ይትፈለጠ፡ መንፈሶሙ፡ ለ*ምዉታን፡ ወከመዝ፡ ተፈልጠ፡ ለመንፈሶሙ፡ ለጻድቃን፡ ዘውእቱ፡ ነቅዐ፡ ማይ፡ በላዕሌሁ፡ ብርህት።", "language": "Geez", "pages": [96], "confidence": "medium", "validation": "unapplied_full_printed_unit_candidate", "note": "Unapplied Charles1906 printed critical-edition candidate after first independent whole-chapter revise/hold review. Recheck actual PDF94–98 including facing apparatus on95 and97; no manuscript or human specialist certification. Bright is a Greek-assisted editor emendation whose syntax remains held for independent review."}, "translation": {"text": "These three[a] were made to separate the spirits of the dead. And thus the spirits of the righteous[b] were separated; above it is a bright spring of water[c].", "philosophy": "optimal-equivalence", "footnotes": [{"marker": "a", "text": "The printed text reads three whereas verse 2 reads four; the two counts are not harmonized.", "reason": "textual_variant"}, {"marker": "b", "text": "Charles note 28 supplies a prefixed preposition with Greek G for the spirits of the righteous; it is an editorial supply.", "reason": "editorial_supply"}, {"marker": "c", "text": "Charles prints emended adjective ብርህት and cites Greek φωτεινή in note 32. Bright provisionally qualifies the spring of water, while above it remains in the English; the exact attachment is difficult.", "reason": "textual_uncertainty"}]}}, {"reference": "1 Enoch 22:10", "source": {"edition": "charles-1906-enoch", "text": "በከመ፡ ከማሁ፡ ተፈጥረ፡ ለኃጥኣን፡ ሶበ፡ ይመውቱ፡ ወይትቀበሩ፡ ውስተ፡ ምድር፡ ወኵነኔ፡ ኢኮነ፡ በላዕሌሆሙ፡ በሕይወቶሙ።", "language": "Geez", "pages": [96], "confidence": "medium", "validation": "unapplied_full_printed_unit_candidate", "note": "Unapplied Charles1906 printed critical-edition candidate after first independent whole-chapter revise/hold review. Recheck actual PDF94–98 including facing apparatus on95 and97; no manuscript or human specialist certification."}, "translation": {"text": "Likewise, a place was made for sinners[a], when they die and are buried in the earth and judgment has not come upon them during their lifetime.", "philosophy": "optimal-equivalence", "footnotes": [{"marker": "a", "text": "A place is supplied from the surrounding description. The comparison introduces sinners discussed further in verse 11; the printed negative concerning judgment remains present.", "reason": "translation_explication"}]}}, {"reference": "1 Enoch 22:11", "source": {"edition": "charles-1906-enoch", "text": "በዝየ፡ ይትፈለጠ፡ ነፍሶሙ፡ ዲበ፡ ዛቲ፡ ዐቢይ፡ ጻዕር፡ እስከ፡ አመ፡ ዐቢይ፡ ዕለት፡ እንተ፡ ኵነኔ፡ ወመቅሠፍት፡ ወጻዕር፡ ለእለ፡ ይረግሙ፡ እስከ፡ ለዓለም፡ ወበቀል፡ ለነፍሶሙ፡ በህየ፡ ይእስሮሙ፡ እስከ፡ ለዓለም፡ [ወእመኒ፡ ውእቱ፡ እምቅድመ፡ ዓለም።]", "language": "Geez", "pages": [96], "confidence": "medium", "validation": "unapplied_full_printed_unit_candidate", "note": "Unapplied Charles1906 printed critical-edition candidate after first independent whole-chapter revise/hold review. Recheck actual PDF94–98 including facing apparatus on95 and97; no manuscript or human specialist certification."}, "translation": {"text": "Here their souls are set apart in this great affliction until the great day of judgment, punishment, and affliction for those who curse forever, and vengeance upon their souls.[a] There he will bind them forever.[b]", "philosophy": "optimal-equivalence", "footnotes": [{"marker": "a", "text": "Those who curse follows the printed active verb. Charles note 41 proposes passive are cursed; that would require an explicit emendation.", "reason": "textual_variant"}, {"marker": "b", "text": "Their souls continue the human sinners in verse 10. The agent of the binding clause is not named in this verse.", "reason": "referent_disclosure"}]}}, {"reference": "1 Enoch 22:12", "source": {"edition": "charles-1906-enoch", "text": "ወከመዝ፡ ተፈልጠ፡ ለነፍስ፡ እለ፡ ይስክዩ፡ እለ፡ ያርእዩ፡ በእንተ፡ ሕጉለት፡ አመ፡ *ተቀትሉ፡ በመዋዕለ፡ ኃጥኣን።", "language": "Geez", "pages": [96], "confidence": "medium", "validation": "unapplied_full_printed_unit_candidate", "note": "Unapplied Charles1906 printed critical-edition candidate after first independent whole-chapter revise/hold review. Recheck actual PDF94–98 including facing apparatus on95 and97; no manuscript or human specialist certification."}, "translation": {"text": "And likewise a division has been made for the souls of those who make accusation[a], who make known their destruction[b] when they were killed in the days of sinners.", "philosophy": "optimal-equivalence", "footnotes": [{"marker": "a", "text": "Or make their complaint; compare the accusation of verses 5–7.", "reason": "lexical_alternative"}, {"marker": "b", "text": "The source names destruction. Their identifies the people already in view; Sheol and anticipated vindication are not explicit here.", "reason": "translation_explication"}]}}, {"reference": "1 Enoch 22:13", "source": {"edition": "charles-1906-enoch", "text": "ወከመዝ፡ ተፈጥረ፡ ለነፍሶሙ፡ ለሰብእ፡ እለ፡ ኢኮኑ፡ ጻድቃነ፡ አላ፡ ኃጥኣነ፡ እለ፡ ፍጹማነ፡ አበሳ፡ ወምስለ፡ አባሲያን፡ ይከውኑ፡ ከማሆሙ፡ ወነፍሶሙሰ፡ ኢትትቀተል፡ በዕለተ፡ ኵነኔ፡ ወኢ*ይትነሥኡ፡ *እምነ፡ ዝየ።", "language": "Geez", "pages": [96, 98], "confidence": "medium", "validation": "unapplied_full_printed_unit_candidate", "note": "Unapplied Charles1906 printed critical-edition candidate after first independent whole-chapter revise/hold review. Recheck actual PDF94–98 including facing apparatus on95 and97; no manuscript or human specialist certification."}, "translation": {"text": "And likewise a place was made for the souls of people who were not righteous but sinners, complete in transgression, and who will be with the transgressors, like them.[a] But their souls will not be killed on the day of judgment, nor will they rise from here.[b]", "philosophy": "optimal-equivalence", "footnotes": [{"marker": "a", "text": "A place is contextual. Like them retains the comparison with the human transgressors and does not identify this group with chapter 21’s imprisoned angels.", "reason": "translation_explication"}, {"marker": "b", "text": "The cross-page continuation separately negates killing of their souls and rising from here. Charles’s notes 1–2 on printed page 60 report variants; this is not a universal doctrine about every soul.", "reason": "textual_variant"}]}}, {"reference": "1 Enoch 22:14", "source": {"edition": "charles-1906-enoch", "text": "ውእተ፡ ጊዜ፡ ባረክዎ፡ ለ*እግዚአ፡ ስብሐት፡ ወእቤ፡ ቡሩክ፡ እግዚአየ፡ እግዚአ፡ ጽድቅ፡ ዘይመልክ፡ እስከ፡ ለዓለም።", "pages": [98], "language": "Geez", "validation": "unapplied_full_printed_unit_candidate", "note": "Unapplied Charles1906 printed critical-edition candidate after first independent whole-chapter revise/hold review. Recheck actual PDF94–98 including facing apparatus on95 and97; no manuscript or human specialist certification."}, "translation": {"text": "At that time I blessed the Lord of Glory and said, “Blessed is my Lord, the Lord of righteousness, who reigns forever.”", "philosophy": "optimal-equivalence", "footnotes": []}}]
